            <ArticleTitle>In-the-bag dislocation of a hydrophilic acrylic intraocular lens.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>848-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of a dislocated hydrophilic acrylic intraocular lens (IOL) inducing astigmatism and causing chronic pain and cystoid macular edema as a result of a folded haptics, which mechanically irritated the iris. Scanning electron micrographs of the explanted IOL, including the capsular bag, showed a folded IOL haptic incarcerated in the capsular bag.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
